# Local Netlify folder
.netlify

# Environment files.
#
# `*.local` above already catches .env.local, which is the one Vite creates -
# and catches nothing else. A plain `.env` was committable in a PUBLIC
# repository, which is the gap this closes. The site's real secrets live in
# the Netlify site environment (CANARY_LOG_KEY, scoped to Functions) and must
# never exist in a tracked file here.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
